**`src/retriever.ts` — what it does**

Exports `retrieve(table, question): { answer: string; evidence: EvidenceCell[] } | null`.

**Item matching** (`findItemByName`): filters table rows whose `name` is a case-sensitive substring of the candidate string extracted from the question template, then keeps only rows with the longest matching name. If that still leaves more than one row, returns `"AMBIGUOUS"` (which the caller converts to `null`).

**Nine question families**, each implemented as a regex that must match the full question string (`^...$`):

| Family | Template | Answer format | Evidence |
|--------|----------|---------------|----------|
| T1 | `Where is <Name> located?` | `location` value | `[{row, "location"}]` |
| T2 | `What is the role of <Name>?` | `role` value | `[{row, "role"}]` |
| T3 | `What is the quantity of <Name>?` | `"<quantity> <unit>"` | `[{row, "quantity"}]` |
| T4 | `What is the hazard class of <Name>?` | `hazard` value | `[{row, "hazard"}]` |
| T5 | `What is <Name> connected to?` | `links` joined with `", "` | `[{row, "links"}]` |
| T6 | `How many items are located in <Location>?` | decimal count string | one `{row, "location"}` per match |
| T7 | `How many items are of type <Type>?` | decimal count string | one `{row, "type"}` per match |
| T8 | `Which has the greater quantity, <NameA> or <NameB>?` | winner's `name` | `[{rowA, "quantity"}, {rowB, "quantity"}]` |
| T9 | `Which item has the role "<Role>"?` | matching item's `name` | `[{row, "role"}]` |

**Returns `null`** when: the question matches no template, a named item isn't in the table, item matching is ambiguous, T6/T7 find no matching rows, T8 quantities are equal or either name is unknown, or T9 matches zero or more than one row.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=173

